1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Compare recordings of the same text. Locate acoustic differences and hear the evidence.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
This is an edited functional walkthrough, not a continuous screen recording.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Two short public-domain weekly addresses supply the reference audio and official transcripts.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Three fixed edit levels preserve the same words while changing pace, pauses, local volume or noise.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hashes, actual sample boundaries and time maps accompany each pair. Word times remain model estimates.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Listen to the unedited reference. The identical-audio control scores 100 with no alert.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The chart follows actual playback. A chosen reference is not a universal rhetorical ideal.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The same text now contains a local tempo edit requesting 2.10× dilation. Listen to the changed phrase.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
The delivery lasts 16.46 seconds, versus 14.84 seconds for the reference.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The fixed rubric reports 65.03 reference similarity, with three grounded alerts.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Play region replays the selected delivery span: 0.90–2.96 seconds, with its word context.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
IMPORTANT lasts 0.64 seconds instead of 0.35: 1.87× the reference duration.

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The advice stays conditional. A deliberate emphasis is a choice, not a diagnosis of speaking ability.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
The edit inserts 0.95 seconds of silence. Alignment estimates a 0.99-second gap before THE.

15
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:42,000
The reference gap is 0.07 seconds: an estimated extra 0.92 seconds. Edit labels and model times are distinct.

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The local amplitude multiplier is 0.22. The shared transcript and clip duration stay unchanged.

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Measured relative energy falls by 12.0 dB after each recording’s median level is removed.

18
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:08,000
The 1.08× tempo request has no matching pace alert. The subtle target is missed.

19
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Two off-target volume alerts remain. A non-perfect score does not establish a correct target hit.

20
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Biden’s 5 dB SNR edit produces noise alerts, but their intervals cover too little of the exact target.

21
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The best matching IoU is 0.224, below the 0.25 target-hit threshold. This pair counts as a miss.

22
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
A global pitch shift with tempo compensation should not create a local-volume warning.

23
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
It does here. The OF alert is the single control false alarm, so normalization is not fully robust.

24
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:49,000
The reported target hits are 16/18 moderate or strong cases and 0/10 near-perfect cases.

25
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:56,000
One of six controls has a false alert. All 34 pairs remain visible, including the misses.

26
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:04,000
The predeclared ≥93% / zero-false-alert gate failed. V2 uses known speakers, not a new blind-speaker test.

27
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Choose two 0.5–30-second audio files, at most 8 MB each, and the same English transcript.

28
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Whisper checks the text, then CTC alignment and acoustic features run on this machine.

29
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
This is the real processing sequence. No audio is sent to a hosted inference service.

30
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,000
The uploaded public example returns 80.47, 46 aligned words and one local-volume region.

31
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:32,000
The server deletes temporary upload files before the reply. Export JSON retains the numerical evidence.

32
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Read-only replay reproduces all 34 recorded analyses from their frozen word times.

33
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Software replay passed; the experiment gate did not. The six-page report keeps that distinction explicit.

34
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Two speakers and controlled edits do not establish general rhetorical or demographic validity.

35
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:00,000
OpenAI Codex assisted with implementation, tests, documentation and demo assembly. No model was trained.

